# Lampang Bus System — Off-host backup sync configuration
#
# Copy to scripts/offhost-backup-sync.env on the production host and
# chmod 600. NEVER commit the real file to git — only this .example.
#
# Pick exactly ONE method by setting OFFHOST_BACKUP_METHOD.

# ─── Method A: rclone ────────────────────────────────────────
# Requires: apt-get install rclone, then `rclone config` to set up
# the named remote (e.g. an S3/B2/GDrive bucket) under
# ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf (mode 600, never committed).
#
# OFFHOST_BACKUP_METHOD=rclone
# OFFHOST_RCLONE_REMOTE=my-remote:lampang-bus-backups/database

# ─── Method B: rsync over SSH ────────────────────────────────
# Requires: an SSH key pair (place private key under ~/.ssh, mode 600)
# whose public key is in authorized_keys on the remote host. The
# remote path must already exist and be writable.
#
# OFFHOST_BACKUP_METHOD=rsync
# OFFHOST_RSYNC_TARGET=backup-user@backup.example.com:/srv/lampang-bus-backups
# OFFHOST_SSH_KEY=/home/schoolbus/.ssh/offhost_id_ed25519

# ─── Common (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Override the local backup source directory (default is fine):
# BACKUP_DIR=/home/schoolbus/backups/lampang-bus
